{"id": "bad_18", "label": 0, "note": "**Breaking API Change**: Changing the method signature from `matches(String name)` to `matches(String... names)` is technically a breaking change. While varargs are backward compatible for single argument calls, this could affect:\n1. Code that uses method references (e.g., `filter::matches`)\n2. Reflection-based code\n3. Lambda expressions that capture this method\n\nConsider:\n- Keeping the old `matches(String name)` method and having it call `matches(name)` for backward compatibility\n- Or document this as a breaking change in the PR description\n\nExample:\n```java\npublic synchronized boolean matches(String name) {\n    return matches(new String[]{name});\n}\n\npublic synchronized boolean matches(String... names) {\n    // current implementation\n}\n```", "path": "plugins/org.jkiss.dbeaver.model/src/org/jkiss/dbeaver/model/struct/DBSObjectFilter.java", "from_line": 153, "to_line": 153, "lang": "Java", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "File Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "Claude-Code/Claude-4.5-Sonnet", "pr_url": "https://github.com/dbeaver/dbeaver/pull/38239", "commit": "ed40132dcb3c6ab5502056b7de0e47c0858ec016", "code": "113\t        this.include = include;\n114\t        this.includePatterns = null;\n115\t    }\n116\t\n117\t    public List<String> getExclude() {\n118\t        return exclude;\n119\t    }\n120\t\n121\t    public void addExclude(String name) {\n122\t        if (exclude == null) {\n123\t            exclude = new ArrayList<>();\n124\t        }\n125\t        if (!exclude.contains(name)) {\n126\t            exclude.add(name);\n127\t        }\n128\t        this.excludePatterns = null;\n129\t    }\n130\t\n131\t    public void setExclude(List<String> exclude) {\n132\t        this.exclude = exclude;\n133\t        this.excludePatterns = null;\n134\t    }\n135\t\n136\t    public boolean isNotApplicable() {\n137\t        return !enabled || isEmpty();\n138\t    }\n139\t\n140\t    public boolean isEmpty() {\n141\t        return CommonUtils.isEmpty(include) && CommonUtils.isEmpty(exclude);\n142\t    }\n143\t\n144\t    public boolean hasSingleMask() {\n145\t        return include != null && include.size() == 1 && CommonUtils.isEmpty(exclude);\n146\t    }\n147\t\n148\t    @Nullable\n149\t    public String getSingleMask() {\n150\t        return !CommonUtils.isEmpty(include) ? include.get(0) : null;\n151\t    }\n152\t\n153\t    public synchronized boolean matches(String... names) {\n154\t        if (includePatterns == null && !CommonUtils.isEmpty(include)) {\n155\t            includePatterns = new ArrayList<>(include.size());\n156\t            for (String inc : include) {\n157\t                if (!inc.isEmpty()) {\n158\t                    includePatterns.add(makePattern(inc, isCaseSensitive()));\n159\t                }\n160\t            }\n161\t        }\n162\t        if (includePatterns != null) {\n163\t            boolean matched = false;\n164\t            for (Object pattern : includePatterns) {\n165\t                if (atLeastOneNameMatchesPattern(pattern, names)) {\n166\t                    matched = true;\n167\t                    break;\n168\t                }\n169\t            }\n170\t            if (!matched) {\n171\t                return false;\n172\t            }\n173\t        }\n174\t\n175\t        if (excludePatterns == null && !CommonUtils.isEmpty(exclude)) {\n176\t            excludePatterns = new ArrayList<>(exclude.size());\n177\t            for (String exc : exclude) {\n178\t                if (!exc.isEmpty()) {\n179\t                    excludePatterns.add(makePattern(exc, isCaseSensitive()));\n180\t                }\n181\t            }\n182\t        }\n183\t        if (excludePatterns != null) {\n184\t            for (Object pattern : excludePatterns) {\n185\t                if (atLeastOneNameMatchesPattern(pattern, names)) {\n186\t                    return false;\n187\t                }\n188\t            }\n189\t        }\n190\t        // Done\n191\t        return true;\n192\t    }\n193\t"}
{"id": "bad_17", "label": 0, "note": "This change makes the logger name dynamic via `fmt::format`. Two concerns:\n1) This file does not explicitly include a fmt header (only `logger_useful.h` etc.). If fmt is currently available only via transitive includes, this can become a fragile build dependency. Consider adding the appropriate fmt include (e.g. `<fmt/format.h>` or the project’s wrapper) in this TU.\n2) Dynamic logger names can increase logger cardinality and may break existing log-level/config rules targeting the stable name `DiskLocal`. If stable config is desired, consider keeping `getLogger(\"DiskLocal\")` and including `name_` in log messages, or use a supported child/logger component mechanism.", "path": "src/Disks/DiskLocal.cpp", "from_line": 537, "to_line": 537, "lang": "C++", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/pull/80391", "commit": "f9d51faa7cba634f38a711494003d404946b05de", "code": "497\t    const std::shared_ptr<IDisk> & to_disk,\n498\t    const String & to_dir,\n499\t    const ReadSettings & read_settings,\n500\t    const WriteSettings & write_settings,\n501\t    const std::function<void()> & cancellation_hook)\n502\t{\n503\t    /// If throttling was configured we cannot use copying directly.\n504\t    if (isSameDiskType(*this, *to_disk) && !read_settings.local_throttler && !write_settings.local_throttler)\n505\t        fs::copy(fs::path(disk_path) / from_dir, fs::path(to_disk->getPath()) / to_dir, fs::copy_options::recursive | fs::copy_options::overwrite_existing); /// Use more optimal way.\n506\t    else\n507\t        IDisk::copyDirectoryContent(from_dir, to_disk, to_dir, read_settings, write_settings, cancellation_hook);\n508\t}\n509\t\n510\tSyncGuardPtr DiskLocal::getDirectorySyncGuard(const String & path) const\n511\t{\n512\t    return std::make_unique<LocalDirectorySyncGuard>(fs::path(disk_path) / path);\n513\t}\n514\t\n515\t\n516\tvoid DiskLocal::applyNewSettings(const Poco::Util::AbstractConfiguration & config, ContextPtr context, const String & config_prefix, const DisksMap & disk_map)\n517\t{\n518\t    String new_disk_path;\n519\t    UInt64 new_keep_free_space_bytes;\n520\t\n521\t    loadDiskLocalConfig(name, config, config_prefix, context, new_disk_path, new_keep_free_space_bytes);\n522\t\n523\t    if (disk_path != new_disk_path)\n524\t        throw Exception(ErrorCodes::UNKNOWN_ELEMENT_IN_CONFIG, \"Disk path can't be updated from config {}\", name);\n525\t\n526\t    if (keep_free_space_bytes != new_keep_free_space_bytes)\n527\t        keep_free_space_bytes = new_keep_free_space_bytes;\n528\t\n529\t    IDisk::applyNewSettings(config, context, config_prefix, disk_map);\n530\t}\n531\t\n532\tDiskLocal::DiskLocal(const String & name_, const String & path_, UInt64 keep_free_space_bytes_,\n533\t                     const Poco::Util::AbstractConfiguration & config, const String & config_prefix)\n534\t    : IDisk(name_, config, config_prefix)\n535\t    , disk_path(path_)\n536\t    , keep_free_space_bytes(keep_free_space_bytes_)\n537\t    , logger(getLogger(fmt::format(\"DiskLocal({})\", name_)))\n538\t    , data_source_description(getLocalDataSourceDescription(disk_path))\n539\t{\n540\t}\n541\t\n542\tDiskLocal::DiskLocal(\n543\t    const String & name_, const String & path_, UInt64 keep_free_space_bytes_, ContextPtr context,\n544\t    const Poco::Util::AbstractConfiguration & config, const String & config_prefix)\n545\t    : DiskLocal(name_, path_, keep_free_space_bytes_, config, config_prefix)\n546\t{\n547\t    auto local_disk_check_period_ms = config.getUInt(\"local_disk_check_period_ms\", 0);\n548\t    if (local_disk_check_period_ms > 0)\n549\t        disk_checker = std::make_unique<DiskLocalCheckThread>(this, context, local_disk_check_period_ms);\n550\t}\n551\t\n552\tDiskLocal::DiskLocal(const String & name_, const String & path_)\n553\t    : IDisk(name_)\n554\t    , disk_path(path_)\n555\t    , keep_free_space_bytes(0)\n556\t    , logger(getLogger(\"DiskLocal\"))\n557\t    , data_source_description(getLocalDataSourceDescription(disk_path))\n558\t{\n559\t}\n560\t\n561\tDataSourceDescription DiskLocal::getDataSourceDescription() const\n562\t{\n563\t    return data_source_description;\n564\t}\n565\t\n566\tDataSourceDescription DiskLocal::getLocalDataSourceDescription(const String & path)\n567\t{\n568\t    DataSourceDescription res;\n569\t    res.type = DataSourceType::Local;\n570\t\n571\t    if (auto block_device_id = tryGetBlockDeviceId(path); block_device_id.has_value())\n572\t        res.description = *block_device_id;\n573\t    else\n574\t        res.description = path;\n575\t    res.is_encrypted = false;\n576\t    res.is_cached = false;\n577\t    return res;"}
{"id": "bad_13", "label": 0, "note": "Only `SubagentTerminateMode.GOAL` is treated as success. If the sub-agent can terminate with other “successful” reasons (e.g., STOP/COMPLETED) in your framework, this may incorrectly mark valid plans as failures. Consider accepting additional terminate reasons or validating presence of `execution_plan` regardless of terminate reason, with a clear fallback error.\n\n```suggestion\n      const plan = plannerAgent.output.emitted_vars['execution_plan'];\n      if (plan) return plan;\n      // optionally check terminate_reason for diagnostics\n      console.error(\n        `Planning sub-agent did not emit execution_plan. terminate_reason=${plannerAgent.output.terminate_reason}`,\n      );\n      return null;\n```", "path": "packages/core/src/tools/planning-tool.ts", "from_line": 210, "to_line": 212, "lang": "TypeScript", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/5819", "commit": "6fd82699700fc19ea30a7b29a059f392ccfbb2cc", "code": "170\t          {\n171\t            functionResponse: {\n172\t              name: planningToolName,\n173\t              response: { success: false, error: 'Invalid JSON response' },\n174\t            },\n175\t          },\n176\t        ],\n177\t        returnDisplay: plan,\n178\t      };\n179\t    }\n180\t  }\n181\t\n182\t  private async createPlan(\n183\t    userRequest: string,\n184\t    onMessage?: (message: string) => void,\n185\t  ): Promise<string | null> {\n186\t    try {\n187\t      const toolConfig: ToolConfig = {\n188\t        tools: [\n189\t          new ReadFileTool(this.runtimeContext),\n190\t          new ReadManyFilesTool(this.runtimeContext),\n191\t          new GrepTool(this.runtimeContext),\n192\t          new GlobTool(this.runtimeContext),\n193\t          new LSTool(this.runtimeContext),\n194\t        ],\n195\t      };\n196\t      const plannerAgent = await SubAgentScope.create(\n197\t        'planning-subagent',\n198\t        this.runtimeContext,\n199\t        promptConfig,\n200\t        modelConfig,\n201\t        runConfig,\n202\t        { outputConfig, onMessage, toolConfig },\n203\t      );\n204\t\n205\t      const context = new ContextState();\n206\t      context.set('user_request', userRequest);\n207\t\n208\t      await plannerAgent.runNonInteractive(context);\n209\t\n210\t      if (plannerAgent.output.terminate_reason === SubagentTerminateMode.GOAL) {\n211\t        return plannerAgent.output.emitted_vars['execution_plan'] || null;\n212\t      }\n213\t\n214\t      console.error(\n215\t        `Planning sub-agent terminated unexpectedly with reason: ${plannerAgent.output.terminate_reason}`,\n216\t      );\n217\t      return null;\n218\t    } catch (error) {\n219\t      console.error('An error occurred while running the PlanningTool:', error);\n220\t      return null;\n221\t    }\n222\t  }\n223\t}\n224\t\n225\texport function getPlanningTool(\n226\t  runtimeContext: Config,\n227\t): BaseTool<{ user_request: string }> {\n228\t  return new PlanningTool(runtimeContext);\n229\t}"}
{"id": "good_10", "label": 1, "note": "The log message format includes the closing bracket in the wrong position. The format string shows `[%s]%s Clearing stack trace` but should be `[%s][%s] Clearing stack trace` to properly match the pattern `[nodeId][indexName][shard]` mentioned in the PR description. \n\nCurrently: `[nodeId][indexName][shard] Clearing stack trace`\nExpected: `[nodeId][indexName][shard] Clearing stack trace`\n\nThe issue is that `request.shardId()` returns a ShardId object which already includes the index name and shard number in its toString() format like `[indexName][shard]`, so the format should be `[%s]%s` (which is correct as written). However, this makes the log format inconsistent with the description that claims it will be prefixed with `[nodeId][indexName][shard]`.", "path": "server/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/search/SearchService.java", "from_line": 558, "to_line": 558, "lang": "Java", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "Claude-Code/Claude-4.5-Sonnet", "pr_url": "https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/125732", "commit": "e38d20c726cffb1ef9563d3146951a5356596464", "code": "518\t\n519\t    @Override\n520\t    protected void doStop() {\n521\t        for (final ReaderContext context : activeReaders.values()) {\n522\t            freeReaderContext(context.id());\n523\t        }\n524\t    }\n525\t\n526\t    @Override\n527\t    protected void doClose() {\n528\t        doStop();\n529\t        keepAliveReaper.cancel();\n530\t    }\n531\t\n532\t    /**\n533\t     * Wraps the listener to avoid sending StackTraces back to the coordinating\n534\t     * node if the `error_trace` header is set to {@code false}. Upon reading we\n535\t     * default to {@code true} to maintain the same behavior as before the change,\n536\t     * due to older nodes not being able to specify whether it needs stack traces.\n537\t     *\n538\t     * @param <T>            the type of the response\n539\t     * @param listener       the action listener to be wrapped\n540\t     * @param request        the shard request being executed\n541\t     * @param threadPool     with context where to write the new header\n542\t     * @param clusterService the cluster service\n543\t     * @return the wrapped action listener\n544\t     */\n545\t    static <T> ActionListener<T> maybeWrapListenerForStackTrace(\n546\t        ActionListener<T> listener,\n547\t        ShardSearchRequest request,\n548\t        ThreadPool threadPool,\n549\t        ClusterService clusterService\n550\t    ) {\n551\t        boolean header = true;\n552\t        if (request.getChannelVersion().onOrAfter(ERROR_TRACE_IN_TRANSPORT_HEADER) && threadPool.getThreadContext() != null) {\n553\t            header = Boolean.parseBoolean(threadPool.getThreadContext().getHeaderOrDefault(\"error_trace\", \"false\"));\n554\t        }\n555\t        if (header == false) {\n556\t            return listener.delegateResponse((l, e) -> {\n557\t                logger.debug(\n558\t                    () -> format(\"[%s]%s Clearing stack trace before transport:\", clusterService.localNode().getId(), request.shardId()),\n559\t                    e\n560\t                );\n561\t                ExceptionsHelper.unwrapCausesAndSuppressed(e, err -> {\n562\t                    err.setStackTrace(EMPTY_STACK_TRACE_ARRAY);\n563\t                    return false;\n564\t                });\n565\t                l.onFailure(e);\n566\t            });\n567\t        }\n568\t        return listener;\n569\t    }\n570\t\n571\t    public void executeDfsPhase(ShardSearchRequest request, SearchShardTask task, ActionListener<SearchPhaseResult> listener) {\n572\t        listener = maybeWrapListenerForStackTrace(listener, request, threadPool, clusterService);\n573\t        final IndexShard shard = getShard(request);\n574\t        rewriteAndFetchShardRequest(shard, request, listener.delegateFailure((l, rewritten) -> {\n575\t            // fork the execution in the search thread pool\n576\t            ensureAfterSeqNoRefreshed(shard, request, () -> executeDfsPhase(request, task), l);\n577\t        }));\n578\t    }\n579\t\n580\t    private DfsSearchResult executeDfsPhase(ShardSearchRequest request, SearchShardTask task) throws IOException {\n581\t        ReaderContext readerContext = createOrGetReaderContext(request);\n582\t        try (@SuppressWarnings(\"unused\") // withScope call is necessary to instrument search execution\n583\t        Releasable scope = tracer.withScope(task);\n584\t            Releasable ignored = readerContext.markAsUsed(getKeepAlive(request));\n585\t            SearchContext context = createContext(readerContext, request, task, ResultsType.DFS, false)\n586\t        ) {\n587\t            DfsPhase.execute(context);\n588\t            return context.dfsResult();\n589\t        } catch (Exception e) {\n590\t            logger.trace(\"Dfs phase failed\", e);\n591\t            processFailure(readerContext, e);\n592\t            throw e;\n593\t        }\n594\t    }\n595\t\n596\t    /**\n597\t     * Try to load the query results from the cache or execute the query phase directly if the cache cannot be used.\n598\t     */"}
{"id": "good_13", "label": 1, "note": "New exported types `Person` and `AssetFace` look like DB record shapes but are defined manually instead of deriving from the actual Kysely/DB schema types (e.g., `Selectable<...>`). This can silently drift from the real DB schema (missing columns, wrong nullability, wrong types). Consider importing the generated DB table types and using `Selectable<DBPerson>` / `Selectable<DBAssetFace>` (or `Insertable/Updateable` as appropriate) to keep types in sync.\n\nAlso, `AssetFace.person?: Person | null;` makes `person` optional *and* nullable, which is usually redundant/ambiguous (property may be missing vs explicitly null). Prefer one representation based on how relations are loaded (e.g., `person: Person | null` when always present on loaded rows, or `person?: Person` when conditionally joined).", "path": "server/src/database.ts", "from_line": 211, "to_line": 239, "lang": "TypeScript", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "File Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/immich-app/immich/pull/17535", "commit": "5f4759196534661bd332085514878d0efbb7ce84", "code": "171\t\n172\texport type AuthSession = {\n173\t  id: string;\n174\t};\n175\t\n176\texport type Partner = {\n177\t  sharedById: string;\n178\t  sharedBy: User;\n179\t  sharedWithId: string;\n180\t  sharedWith: User;\n181\t  createdAt: Date;\n182\t  updatedAt: Date;\n183\t  updateId: string;\n184\t  inTimeline: boolean;\n185\t};\n186\t\n187\texport type Place = {\n188\t  admin1Code: string | null;\n189\t  admin1Name: string | null;\n190\t  admin2Code: string | null;\n191\t  admin2Name: string | null;\n192\t  alternateNames: string | null;\n193\t  countryCode: string;\n194\t  id: number;\n195\t  latitude: number;\n196\t  longitude: number;\n197\t  modificationDate: Date;\n198\t  name: string;\n199\t};\n200\t\n201\texport type Session = {\n202\t  id: string;\n203\t  createdAt: Date;\n204\t  updatedAt: Date;\n205\t  deviceOS: string;\n206\t  deviceType: string;\n207\t};\n208\t\n209\texport type Exif = Omit<Selectable<DatabaseExif>, 'updatedAt' | 'updateId'>;\n210\t\n211\texport type Person = {\n212\t  createdAt: Date;\n213\t  id: string;\n214\t  ownerId: string;\n215\t  updatedAt: Date;\n216\t  updateId: string;\n217\t  isFavorite: boolean;\n218\t  name: string;\n219\t  birthDate: Date | null;\n220\t  color: string | null;\n221\t  faceAssetId: string | null;\n222\t  isHidden: boolean;\n223\t  thumbnailPath: string;\n224\t};\n225\t\n226\texport type AssetFace = {\n227\t  id: string;\n228\t  deletedAt: Date | null;\n229\t  assetId: string;\n230\t  boundingBoxX1: number;\n231\t  boundingBoxX2: number;\n232\t  boundingBoxY1: number;\n233\t  boundingBoxY2: number;\n234\t  imageHeight: number;\n235\t  imageWidth: number;\n236\t  personId: string | null;\n237\t  sourceType: SourceType;\n238\t  person?: Person | null;\n239\t};\n240\t\n241\tconst userColumns = ['id', 'name', 'email', 'profileImagePath', 'profileChangedAt'] as const;\n242\t\n243\texport const columns = {\n244\t  authUser: [\n245\t    'users.id',\n246\t    'users.name',\n247\t    'users.email',\n248\t    'users.isAdmin',\n249\t    'users.quotaUsageInBytes',\n250\t    'users.quotaSizeInBytes',\n251\t  ],\n252\t  authApiKey: ['api_keys.id', 'api_keys.permissions'],\n253\t  authSession: ['sessions.id', 'sessions.updatedAt'],\n254\t  authSharedLink: [\n255\t    'shared_links.id',\n256\t    'shared_links.userId',\n257\t    'shared_links.expiresAt',\n258\t    'shared_links.showExif',\n259\t    'shared_links.allowUpload',\n260\t    'shared_links.allowDownload',\n261\t    'shared_links.password',\n262\t  ],\n263\t  user: userColumns,\n264\t  userWithPrefix: ['users.id', 'users.name', 'users.email', 'users.profileImagePath', 'users.profileChangedAt'],\n265\t  userAdmin: [\n266\t    ...userColumns,\n267\t    'createdAt',\n268\t    'updatedAt',\n269\t    'deletedAt',\n270\t    'isAdmin',\n271\t    'status',\n272\t    'oauthId',\n273\t    'profileImagePath',\n274\t    'shouldChangePassword',\n275\t    'storageLabel',\n276\t    'quotaSizeInBytes',\n277\t    'quotaUsageInBytes',\n278\t  ],\n279\t  tagDto: ['id', 'value', 'createdAt', 'updatedAt', 'color', 'parentId'],"}
{"id": "good_02", "label": 1, "note": "`#[allow(dead_code)]` was added on `deserialize_option`. If this is only needed for certain feature combinations/tests, prefer gating the function itself with `#[cfg(...)]` or using a more specific allow (e.g., `#[cfg_attr(not(test), allow(dead_code))]`) to avoid masking genuinely unused code in production builds.", "path": "crates/api_models/src/payments.rs", "from_line": 7630, "to_line": 7633, "lang": "Rust", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/juspay/hyperswitch/pull/7353", "commit": "59ec03ceef191dcada50380ec20cd843b80a87b6", "code": "7590\t        }\n7591\t    }\n7592\t\n7593\t    impl<'de> Visitor<'de> for OptionalPaymentIdVisitor {\n7594\t        type Value = Option<PaymentIdType>;\n7595\t\n7596\t        fn expecting(&self, formatter: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {\n7597\t            formatter.write_str(\"payment id\")\n7598\t        }\n7599\t\n7600\t        fn visit_some<D>(self, deserializer: D) -> Result<Self::Value, D::Error>\n7601\t        where\n7602\t            D: Deserializer<'de>,\n7603\t        {\n7604\t            deserializer.deserialize_any(PaymentIdVisitor).map(Some)\n7605\t        }\n7606\t\n7607\t        fn visit_none<E>(self) -> Result<Self::Value, E>\n7608\t        where\n7609\t            E: de::Error,\n7610\t        {\n7611\t            Ok(None)\n7612\t        }\n7613\t\n7614\t        fn visit_unit<E>(self) -> Result<Self::Value, E>\n7615\t        where\n7616\t            E: de::Error,\n7617\t        {\n7618\t            Ok(None)\n7619\t        }\n7620\t    }\n7621\t\n7622\t    #[allow(dead_code)]\n7623\t    pub(crate) fn deserialize<'a, D>(deserializer: D) -> Result<PaymentIdType, D::Error>\n7624\t    where\n7625\t        D: Deserializer<'a>,\n7626\t    {\n7627\t        deserializer.deserialize_any(PaymentIdVisitor)\n7628\t    }\n7629\t\n7630\t    #[allow(dead_code)]\n7631\t    pub(crate) fn deserialize_option<'a, D>(\n7632\t        deserializer: D,\n7633\t    ) -> Result<Option<PaymentIdType>, D::Error>\n7634\t    where\n7635\t        D: Deserializer<'a>,\n7636\t    {\n7637\t        deserializer.deserialize_option(OptionalPaymentIdVisitor)\n7638\t    }\n7639\t}\n7640\t\n7641\t#[cfg(feature = \"v1\")]\n7642\tmod payment_id_type {\n7643\t    use std::{borrow::Cow, fmt};\n7644\t\n7645\t    use serde::{\n7646\t        de::{self, Visitor},\n7647\t        Deserializer,\n7648\t    };\n7649\t\n7650\t    use super::PaymentIdType;\n7651\t\n7652\t    struct PaymentIdVisitor;\n7653\t    struct OptionalPaymentIdVisitor;\n7654\t\n7655\t    impl Visitor<'_> for PaymentIdVisitor {\n7656\t        type Value = PaymentIdType;\n7657\t\n7658\t        fn expecting(&self, formatter: &mut fmt::Formatter<'_>) -> fmt::Result {\n7659\t            formatter.write_str(\"payment id\")\n7660\t        }\n7661\t\n7662\t        fn visit_str<E>(self, value: &str) -> Result<Self::Value, E>\n7663\t        where\n7664\t            E: de::Error,\n7665\t        {\n7666\t            common_utils::id_type::PaymentId::try_from(Cow::Owned(value.to_string()))\n7667\t                .map_err(de::Error::custom)\n7668\t                .map(PaymentIdType::PaymentIntentId)\n7669\t        }\n7670\t    }\n7671\t\n7672\t    impl<'de> Visitor<'de> for OptionalPaymentIdVisitor {\n7673\t        type Value = Option<PaymentIdType>;"}
{"id": "good_12", "label": 1, "note": "Good refactoring - moving tensor creation closer to where it's used. The code now creates `batchPositions` and `batchOutputs` as slices first, then converts them to tensors just before the Forward call. This is cleaner and more efficient. However, ensure that the `ctx.Input()` calls for creating tensors don't fail silently if the context is invalid.", "path": "runner/ollamarunner/runner.go", "from_line": 581, "to_line": 581, "lang": "Go", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "File Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "Claude-Code/Claude-4.5-Sonnet", "pr_url": "https://github.com/ollama/ollama/pull/12185", "commit": "b6002f6b6c69370f8c18a9e6c1cafa8463273a6b", "code": "541\t\n542\t\t\t\tbatchInputs = append(batchInputs, seq.inputs[i])\n543\t\t\t\tif inp.Multimodal != nil {\n544\t\t\t\t\tvar mm []input.Multimodal\n545\t\t\t\t\tmm, err = seq.mmStore.getMultimodal(s.model.Backend(), nextBatch.ctx, inp.Multimodal, false)\n546\t\t\t\t\tif err != nil {\n547\t\t\t\t\t\treturn\n548\t\t\t\t\t}\n549\t\t\t\t\tbatch.Multimodal = append(batch.Multimodal, input.MultimodalIndex{Index: len(batchInputs) - 1, Multimodal: mm})\n550\t\t\t\t}\n551\t\n552\t\t\t\tbatchPositions = append(batchPositions, int32(len(seq.cache.Inputs)+len(seq.pendingInputs)))\n553\t\t\t\tbatch.Sequences = append(batch.Sequences, seq.cache.Id)\n554\t\n555\t\t\t\tseq.iBatch = len(batchOutputs)\n556\t\t\t\tif i+1 == len(seq.inputs) {\n557\t\t\t\t\tbatchOutputs = append(batchOutputs, int32(len(batchInputs)-1))\n558\t\t\t\t}\n559\t\t\t\tlogutil.Trace(\"forwardBatch iBatch\", \"batchID\", s.batchID, \"seqIdx\", seqIdx, \"seq.iBatch\", seq.iBatch, \"i+1\", i+1, \"len(seq.inputs)\", len(seq.inputs))\n560\t\t\t\tseq.pendingInputs = append(seq.pendingInputs, inp)\n561\t\t\t}\n562\t\n563\t\t\tseq.inputs = seq.inputs[len(seq.pendingInputs):]\n564\t\t}\n565\t\n566\t\tif resumeSeq != -1 {\n567\t\t\ts.nextSeq = resumeSeq\n568\t\t} else {\n569\t\t\ts.nextSeq = seqIdx + 1\n570\t\t}\n571\t\n572\t\tif len(batchInputs) == 0 {\n573\t\t\tlogutil.Trace(\"forwardBatch no batchInputs, going idle\", \"batchID\", s.batchID)\n574\t\t\tnextBatch.ctx.Close()\n575\t\t\tnextBatch.ctx = nil\n576\t\t\treturn\n577\t\t}\n578\t\ts.batchID++\n579\t\n580\t\t// Actual batchInputs values will be injected into the batch.Inputs tensor before calling Compute\n581\t\tbatch.Inputs = nextBatch.ctx.Input().Empty(ml.DTypeI32, len(batchInputs))\n582\t\tbatch.Positions = nextBatch.ctx.Input().FromIntSlice(batchPositions, len(batchPositions))\n583\t\tbatch.Outputs = nextBatch.ctx.Input().FromIntSlice(batchOutputs, len(batchOutputs))\n584\t\tnextBatch.modelOutput, err = model.Forward(nextBatch.ctx, s.model, batch)\n585\t\tif err != nil {\n586\t\t\terr = fmt.Errorf(\"failed to build graph: %w\", err)\n587\t\t\treturn\n588\t\t}\n589\t\tnextBatch.batchInputs = batchInputs\n590\t\tnextBatch.batch = batch\n591\t\n592\t\treturn\n593\t}\n594\t\n595\t// Async processing of the next batch\n596\tfunc (s *Server) computeBatch(activeBatch batchState) {\n597\t\tif activeBatch.ctx == nil {\n598\t\t\t// Nothing to compute\n599\t\t\treturn\n600\t\t}\n601\t\tdefer activeBatch.ctx.Close()\n602\t\n603\t\t// Wait until inputs are ready\n604\t\tlogutil.Trace(\"computeBatch: waiting for inputs to be ready\", \"batchID\", activeBatch.id)\n605\t\t<-activeBatch.inputsReadyCh\n606\t\tlogutil.Trace(\"computeBatch: inputs are ready\", \"batchID\", activeBatch.id)\n607\t\n608\t\t// Once we complete, signal the next batch of inputs are ready\n609\t\t// This will unblock the next computeBatch, or forwardBatch if new seqs come in\n610\t\tdefer func() {\n611\t\t\tlogutil.Trace(\"computeBatch: outputs are ready\", \"batchID\", activeBatch.id)\n612\t\t\tactiveBatch.outputsReadyCh <- struct{}{}\n613\t\t}()\n614\t\n615\t\ts.mu.Lock()\n616\t\n617\t\t// Gather the actual input token values now that they're ready\n618\t\tbatchInputs := make([]int32, len(activeBatch.batchInputs))\n619\t\tfor i := range batchInputs {\n620\t\t\tbatchInputs[i] = activeBatch.batchInputs[i].Token\n621\t\t}"}
{"id": "good_05", "label": 1, "note": "New line unconditionally dereferences `appConfig` (`appConfig.MachineTag`). If `appConfig` can ever be nil (e.g., miswired endpoint, tests, older call sites), this will panic and break the endpoint. Consider guarding `appConfig != nil` and optionally skipping the header when MachineTag is empty to avoid sending an empty header value.\n\n```suggestion\n\t\tif appConfig != nil && appConfig.MachineTag != \"\" {\n\t\t\tc.Set(\"LocalAI-Machine-Tag\", appConfig.MachineTag)\n\t\t}\n```", "path": "core/http/endpoints/jina/rerank.go", "from_line": 22, "to_line": 22, "lang": "Go", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/mudler/LocalAI/pull/4577", "commit": "e466450c007539a2b1e4d2951c6756ff004a2b52", "code": "1\tpackage jina\n2\t\n3\timport (\n4\t\t\"github.com/mudler/LocalAI/core/backend\"\n5\t\t\"github.com/mudler/LocalAI/core/config\"\n6\t\n7\t\t\"github.com/gofiber/fiber/v2\"\n8\t\tfiberContext \"github.com/mudler/LocalAI/core/http/ctx\"\n9\t\t\"github.com/mudler/LocalAI/core/schema\"\n10\t\t\"github.com/mudler/LocalAI/pkg/grpc/proto\"\n11\t\t\"github.com/mudler/LocalAI/pkg/model\"\n12\t\t\"github.com/rs/zerolog/log\"\n13\t)\n14\t\n15\t// JINARerankEndpoint acts like the Jina reranker endpoint (https://jina.ai/reranker/)\n16\t// @Summary Reranks a list of phrases by relevance to a given text query.\n17\t// @Param request body schema.JINARerankRequest true \"query params\"\n18\t// @Success 200 {object} schema.JINARerankResponse \"Response\"\n19\t// @Router /v1/rerank [post]\n20\tfunc JINARerankEndpoint(cl *config.BackendConfigLoader, ml *model.ModelLoader, appConfig *config.ApplicationConfig) func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n21\t\treturn func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n22\t\t\tc.Set(\"LocalAI-Machine-Tag\", appConfig.MachineTag)\n23\t\n24\t\t\treq := new(schema.JINARerankRequest)\n25\t\t\tif err := c.BodyParser(req); err != nil {\n26\t\t\t\treturn c.Status(fiber.StatusBadRequest).JSON(fiber.Map{\n27\t\t\t\t\t\"error\": \"Cannot parse JSON\",\n28\t\t\t\t})\n29\t\t\t}\n30\t\n31\t\t\tinput := new(schema.TTSRequest)\n32\t\n33\t\t\t// Get input data from the request body\n34\t\t\tif err := c.BodyParser(input); err != nil {\n35\t\t\t\treturn err\n36\t\t\t}\n37\t\n38\t\t\tmodelFile, err := fiberContext.ModelFromContext(c, cl, ml, input.Model, false)\n39\t\t\tif err != nil {\n40\t\t\t\tmodelFile = input.Model\n41\t\t\t\tlog.Warn().Msgf(\"Model not found in context: %s\", input.Model)\n42\t\t\t}\n43\t\n44\t\t\tcfg, err := cl.LoadBackendConfigFileByName(modelFile, appConfig.ModelPath,\n45\t\t\t\tconfig.LoadOptionDebug(appConfig.Debug),\n46\t\t\t\tconfig.LoadOptionThreads(appConfig.Threads),\n47\t\t\t\tconfig.LoadOptionContextSize(appConfig.ContextSize),\n48\t\t\t\tconfig.LoadOptionF16(appConfig.F16),\n49\t\t\t)\n50\t\t\tif err != nil {\n51\t\t\t\tmodelFile = input.Model\n52\t\t\t\tlog.Warn().Msgf(\"Model not found in context: %s\", input.Model)\n53\t\t\t} else {\n54\t\t\t\tmodelFile = cfg.Model\n55\t\t\t}\n56\t\n57\t\t\tlog.Debug().Msgf(\"Request for model: %s\", modelFile)\n58\t\n59\t\t\tif input.Backend != \"\" {\n60\t\t\t\tcfg.Backend = input.Backend\n61\t\t\t}\n62\t"}
{"id": "good_19", "label": 1, "note": "The pagination loop lacks a safeguard against infinite iteration. If entries are being added to the `received_log` faster than the client paginates through it (e.g., during concurrent writes), the condition `received_entries < CHAIN_INFO_MAX_RECEIVED_LOG_ENTRIES` might never be met, potentially causing an infinite loop.\n\nConsider adding a maximum iteration limit or a timeout safeguard to prevent this edge case. For example:\n```rust\nlet mut iterations = 0;\nconst MAX_ITERATIONS: u32 = 1000;\nloop {\n    let query = ChainInfoQuery::new(chain_id).with_received_log_excluding_first_n(offset);\n    let info = remote_node.handle_chain_info_query(query).await?;\n    let received_entries = info.requested_received_log.len();\n    offset += received_entries as u64;\n    remote_log.extend(info.requested_received_log);\n    if received_entries < CHAIN_INFO_MAX_RECEIVED_LOG_ENTRIES {\n        break;\n    }\n    iterations += 1;\n    if iterations >= MAX_ITERATIONS {\n        warn!(\"Reached maximum iterations while paginating received log for chain {:?}\", chain_id);\n        break;\n    }\n}\n```", "path": "linera-core/src/client/mod.rs", "from_line": 846, "to_line": 857, "lang": "Rust", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GLM-4.7", "pr_url": "https://github.com/linera-io/linera-protocol/pull/4639", "commit": "3535ddb83de7dfae5db1732a7f1535031d31380a", "code": "806\t                        blob_ids,\n807\t                        &nodes,\n808\t                        self.options.blob_download_timeout,\n809\t                    )\n810\t                    .await\n811\t                    .ok_or(err)?;\n812\t                    self.local_node.store_blobs(&blobs).await?;\n813\t                    self.handle_certificate(certificate.clone()).await?;\n814\t                }\n815\t                _ => {\n816\t                    // The certificate is not as expected. Give up.\n817\t                    warn!(\"Failed to process network hashed certificate value\");\n818\t                    return Err(err.into());\n819\t                }\n820\t            }\n821\t        }\n822\t\n823\t        Ok(())\n824\t    }\n825\t\n826\t    /// Downloads and preprocesses all confirmed block certificates that sent any message to this\n827\t    /// chain.\n828\t    #[instrument(level = \"trace\", skip(self))]\n829\t    async fn synchronize_received_certificates_from_validator(\n830\t        &self,\n831\t        chain_id: ChainId,\n832\t        remote_node: &RemoteNode<Env::ValidatorNode>,\n833\t    ) -> Result<ReceivedCertificatesFromValidator, ChainClientError> {\n834\t        let mut tracker = self\n835\t            .local_node\n836\t            .chain_state_view(chain_id)\n837\t            .await?\n838\t            .received_certificate_trackers\n839\t            .get()\n840\t            .get(&remote_node.public_key)\n841\t            .copied()\n842\t            .unwrap_or(0);\n843\t        let (max_epoch, committees) = self.admin_committees().await?;\n844\t\n845\t        // Retrieve the list of newly received certificates from this validator.\n846\t        let mut remote_log = Vec::new();\n847\t        let mut offset = tracker;\n848\t        loop {\n849\t            let query = ChainInfoQuery::new(chain_id).with_received_log_excluding_first_n(offset);\n850\t            let info = remote_node.handle_chain_info_query(query).await?;\n851\t            let received_entries = info.requested_received_log.len();\n852\t            offset += received_entries as u64;\n853\t            remote_log.extend(info.requested_received_log);\n854\t            if received_entries < CHAIN_INFO_MAX_RECEIVED_LOG_ENTRIES {\n855\t                break;\n856\t            }\n857\t        }\n858\t        let remote_heights = Self::heights_per_chain(&remote_log);\n859\t\n860\t        // Obtain the next block height we need in the local node, for each chain.\n861\t        let local_next_heights = self\n862\t            .local_node\n863\t            .next_outbox_heights(remote_heights.keys(), chain_id)\n864\t            .await?;\n865\t\n866\t        // We keep track of the height we've successfully downloaded and checked, per chain.\n867\t        let mut downloaded_heights = BTreeMap::new();\n868\t        // And we make a list of chains we already fully have locally. We need to make sure to\n869\t        // put all their sent messages into the inbox.\n870\t        let mut other_sender_chains = Vec::new();\n871\t\n872\t        let certificates = future::try_join_all(remote_heights.into_iter().filter_map(\n873\t            |(sender_chain_id, remote_heights)| {\n874\t                let local_next = *local_next_heights.get(&sender_chain_id)?;\n875\t                if let Ok(height) = local_next.try_sub_one() {\n876\t                    downloaded_heights.insert(sender_chain_id, height);\n877\t                }\n878\t                let remote_heights = remote_heights\n879\t                    .into_iter()\n880\t                    .filter(|h| *h >= local_next)\n881\t                    .collect::<Vec<_>>();\n882\t                if remote_heights.is_empty() {\n883\t                    // Our highest, locally executed block is higher than any block height\n884\t                    // from the current batch. Skip this batch, but remember to wait for\n885\t                    // the messages to be delivered to the inboxes.\n886\t                    other_sender_chains.push(sender_chain_id);\n887\t                    return None;\n888\t                };\n889\t                Some(async move {\n890\t                    let certificates = remote_node\n891\t                        .download_certificates_by_heights(sender_chain_id, remote_heights)\n892\t                        .await?;\n893\t                    Ok::<Vec<_>, ChainClientError>(certificates)\n894\t                })\n895\t            },\n896\t        ))\n897\t        .await?"}
{"id": "good_14", "label": 1, "note": "Direct assignment modifies the original object. Consider creating a deep copy to prevent unintended side effects.\n", "path": "packages/cli/src/utils/commentJson.ts", "from_line": 56, "to_line": 56, "lang": "TypeScript", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "Qwen-Coder-480B", "pr_url": "https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/8154", "commit": "0fa1bd7ac417366f321ed2554caeaef550321959", "code": "16\t/**\n17\t * Updates a JSON file while preserving comments, formatting, and environment variable references.\n18\t */\n19\texport function updateSettingsFilePreservingFormat(\n20\t  filePath: string,\n21\t  updates: Record<string, unknown>,\n22\t  envVarMappings: EnvVarMapping[] = [],\n23\t): void {\n24\t  if (!fs.existsSync(filePath)) {\n25\t    fs.writeFileSync(filePath, JSON.stringify(updates, null, 2), 'utf-8');\n26\t    return;\n27\t  }\n28\t\n29\t  const originalContent = fs.readFileSync(filePath, 'utf-8');\n30\t\n31\t  let parsed: Record<string, unknown>;\n32\t  try {\n33\t    parsed = parse(originalContent) as Record<string, unknown>;\n34\t  } catch (error) {\n35\t    console.error('Error parsing settings file:', error);\n36\t    console.error(\n37\t      'Settings file may be corrupted. Please check the JSON syntax.',\n38\t    );\n39\t    return;\n40\t  }\n41\t\n42\t  const updatedStructure = applyUpdates(parsed, updates);\n43\t  const restoredStructure = restoreEnvVarReferences(\n44\t    updatedStructure,\n45\t    envVarMappings,\n46\t  );\n47\t  const updatedContent = stringify(restoredStructure, null, 2);\n48\t\n49\t  fs.writeFileSync(filePath, updatedContent, 'utf-8');\n50\t}\n51\t\n52\tfunction applyUpdates(\n53\t  current: Record<string, unknown>,\n54\t  updates: Record<string, unknown>,\n55\t): Record<string, unknown> {\n56\t  const result = current;\n57\t\n58\t  for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(updates)) {\n59\t    // Prevent prototype pollution\n60\t    if (key === '__proto__' || key === 'constructor' || key === 'prototype') {\n61\t      continue;\n62\t    }\n63\t    if (\n64\t      typeof value === 'object' &&\n65\t      value !== null &&\n66\t      !Array.isArray(value) &&\n67\t      typeof result[key] === 'object' &&\n68\t      result[key] !== null &&\n69\t      !Array.isArray(result[key])\n70\t    ) {\n71\t      result[key] = applyUpdates(\n72\t        result[key] as Record<string, unknown>,\n73\t        value as Record<string, unknown>,\n74\t      );\n75\t    } else {\n76\t      result[key] = value;\n77\t    }\n78\t  }\n79\t\n80\t  return result;\n81\t}\n82\t\n83\tfunction restoreEnvVarReferences(\n84\t  obj: Record<string, unknown>,\n85\t  envVarMappings: EnvVarMapping[],\n86\t): Record<string, unknown> {\n87\t  if (envVarMappings.length === 0) {\n88\t    return obj;\n89\t  }\n90\t\n91\t  const envVarMap = new Map<string, string>();\n92\t  for (const mapping of envVarMappings) {\n93\t    const pathStr = mapping.path.join('.');\n94\t    envVarMap.set(pathStr, mapping.originalValue);\n95\t  }\n96\t"}
{"id": "good_20", "label": 1, "note": "The macro `valkey_build_and_install_module` is unused in the codebase and should be removed, as confirmed by `git grep` showing no references beyond its definition. The added RDMA dependency logic within it is unnecessary since the macro is never invoked.", "path": "cmake/Modules/ValkeySetup.cmake", "from_line": 127, "to_line": 127, "lang": "C", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": false, "source_model": "", "pr_url": "https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey/pull/2059", "commit": "1379171021c18b009fa02c42088e82caf0e33203", "code": "87\t    if (USE_TLS)\n88\t        # Add required libraries needed for TLS\n89\t        target_link_libraries(${target} OpenSSL::SSL valkey::valkey_tls)\n90\t    endif ()\n91\t\n92\t    if (USE_RDMA)\n93\t        # Add required libraries needed for RDMA\n94\t        target_link_libraries(${target} valkey::valkey_rdma valkey::valkey)\n95\t    endif ()\n96\t\n97\t    if (IS_FREEBSD)\n98\t        target_link_libraries(${target} execinfo)\n99\t    endif ()\n100\t\n101\t    # Enable all warnings + fail on warning\n102\t    target_compile_options(${target} PRIVATE -Werror -Wall)\n103\t\n104\t    # Install cli tool and create a redis symbolic link\n105\t    valkey_install_bin(${target})\n106\t    valkey_create_symlink(${target} ${link_name})\n107\tendmacro ()\n108\t\n109\t# Helper function that defines, builds and installs `target` module.\n110\tmacro (valkey_build_and_install_module target sources ld_flags libs)\n111\t    add_library(${target} SHARED ${sources})\n112\t\n113\t    if (USE_JEMALLOC)\n114\t        # Using jemalloc\n115\t        target_link_libraries(${target} jemalloc)\n116\t    endif ()\n117\t\n118\t    # Place this line last to ensure that ${ld_flags} is placed last on the linker line\n119\t    target_link_libraries(${target} ${libs} ${ld_flags})\n120\t    if (USE_TLS)\n121\t        # Add required libraries needed for TLS\n122\t        target_link_libraries(${target} OpenSSL::SSL valkey::valkey_tls)\n123\t    endif ()\n124\t\n125\t    if (USE_RDMA)\n126\t        # Add required libraries needed for RDMA\n127\t        target_link_libraries(${target} valkey::valkey_rdma valkey::valkey)\n128\t    endif ()\n129\t\n130\t    if (IS_FREEBSD)\n131\t        target_link_libraries(${target} execinfo)\n132\t    endif ()\n133\t\n134\t    # Install cli tool and create a redis symbolic link\n135\t    valkey_install_bin(${target})\n136\tendmacro ()\n137\t\n138\t# Determine if we are building in Release or Debug mode\n139\tif (CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE MATCHES Debug OR CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE MATCHES DebugFull)\n140\t    set(VALKEY_DEBUG_BUILD 1)\n141\t    set(VALKEY_RELEASE_BUILD 0)\n142\t    message(STATUS \"Building in debug mode\")\n143\telse ()\n144\t    set(VALKEY_DEBUG_BUILD 0)\n145\t    set(VALKEY_RELEASE_BUILD 1)\n146\t    message(STATUS \"Building in release mode\")\n147\tendif ()\n148\t\n149\t# ----------------------------------------------------\n150\t# Helper functions - end\n151\t# ----------------------------------------------------\n152\t\n153\t# ----------------------------------------------------\n154\t# Build options (allocator, tls, rdma et al)\n155\t# ----------------------------------------------------\n156\t\n157\tif (NOT BUILD_MALLOC)\n158\t    if (APPLE)\n159\t        set(BUILD_MALLOC \"libc\")\n160\t    elseif (UNIX)\n161\t        set(BUILD_MALLOC \"jemalloc\")\n162\t    endif ()\n163\tendif ()\n164\t\n165\t# User may pass different allocator library. Using -DBUILD_MALLOC=<libname>, make sure it is a valid value\n166\tif (BUILD_MALLOC)\n167\t    if (\"${BUILD_MALLOC}\" STREQUAL \"jemalloc\")"}
{"id": "bad_15", "label": 0, "note": "The function silently ignores `rdma=1` requests when compiled without RDMA support (USE_RDMA undefined), risking incorrect behavior; add error handling (e.g., `assert(!rdma)`) in the `#else` branch to prevent silent failures.", "path": "src/cli_common.c", "from_line": 438, "to_line": 438, "lang": "C", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "File Level", "is_ai_comment": false, "source_model": "", "pr_url": "https://github.com/valkey-io/valkey/pull/2059", "commit": "1379171021c18b009fa02c42088e82caf0e33203", "code": "398\t/*\n399\t * Escape a Unicode string for JSON output (--json), following RFC 7159:\n400\t * https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc7159#section-7\n401\t */\n402\tsds escapeJsonString(sds s, const char *p, size_t len) {\n403\t    s = sdscatlen(s, \"\\\"\", 1);\n404\t    while (len--) {\n405\t        switch (*p) {\n406\t        case '\\\\':\n407\t        case '\"': s = sdscatprintf(s, \"\\\\%c\", *p); break;\n408\t        case '\\n': s = sdscatlen(s, \"\\\\n\", 2); break;\n409\t        case '\\f': s = sdscatlen(s, \"\\\\f\", 2); break;\n410\t        case '\\r': s = sdscatlen(s, \"\\\\r\", 2); break;\n411\t        case '\\t': s = sdscatlen(s, \"\\\\t\", 2); break;\n412\t        case '\\b': s = sdscatlen(s, \"\\\\b\", 2); break;\n413\t        default: s = sdscatprintf(s, *(unsigned char *)p <= 0x1f ? \"\\\\u%04x\" : \"%c\", *p);\n414\t        }\n415\t        p++;\n416\t    }\n417\t    return sdscatlen(s, \"\\\"\", 1);\n418\t}\n419\t\n420\tsds cliVersion(void) {\n421\t    sds version = sdscatprintf(sdsempty(), \"%s\", VALKEY_VERSION);\n422\t\n423\t    /* Add git commit and working tree status when available. */\n424\t    if (strtoll(serverGitSHA1(), NULL, 16)) {\n425\t        version = sdscatprintf(version, \" (git:%s\", serverGitSHA1());\n426\t        if (strtoll(serverGitDirty(), NULL, 10)) version = sdscatprintf(version, \"-dirty\");\n427\t        version = sdscat(version, \")\");\n428\t    }\n429\t    return version;\n430\t}\n431\t\n432\t/* This is a wrapper to call valkeyConnect or valkeyConnectWithTimeout. */\n433\tvalkeyContext *valkeyConnectWrapper(const char *ip, int port, const struct timeval tv, int nonblock, int rdma) {\n434\t    valkeyOptions options = {0};\n435\t    if (rdma) {\n436\t#ifdef USE_RDMA\n437\t        VALKEY_OPTIONS_SET_RDMA(&options, ip, port);\n438\t#endif\n439\t    } else {\n440\t        VALKEY_OPTIONS_SET_TCP(&options, ip, port);\n441\t    }\n442\t\n443\t    if (tv.tv_sec || tv.tv_usec) {\n444\t        options.connect_timeout = &tv;\n445\t    }\n446\t\n447\t    if (nonblock) {\n448\t        options.options |= VALKEY_OPT_NONBLOCK;\n449\t    }\n450\t\n451\t    return valkeyConnectWithOptions(&options);\n452\t}\n453\t\n454\t/* This is a wrapper to call valkeyConnectUnix or valkeyConnectUnixWithTimeout. */\n455\tvalkeyContext *valkeyConnectUnixWrapper(const char *path, const struct timeval tv, int nonblock) {\n456\t    valkeyOptions options = {0};\n457\t    VALKEY_OPTIONS_SET_UNIX(&options, path);\n458\t\n459\t    if (tv.tv_sec || tv.tv_usec) {\n460\t        options.connect_timeout = &tv;\n461\t    }\n462\t\n463\t    if (nonblock) {\n464\t        options.options |= VALKEY_OPT_NONBLOCK;\n465\t    }\n466\t\n467\t    return valkeyConnectWithOptions(&options);\n468\t}"}
{"id": "bad_09", "label": 0, "note": "The loop uses an unnamed tuple with `std::get<index>` for model data, reducing readability; replace with a struct (e.g., `modelInfo`) containing named fields (`uuid`, `path`, `filename`) for clarity.", "path": "src/Mod/Material/App/ModelLibrary.cpp", "from_line": 77, "to_line": 79, "lang": "C++", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": false, "source_model": "", "pr_url": "https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/20825", "commit": "870d7f5385af5d377994479ce6ad017465bdad3d", "code": "37\tusing namespace Materials;\n38\t\n39\tTYPESYSTEM_SOURCE(Materials::ModelLibrary, Materials::Library)\n40\t\n41\tModelLibrary::ModelLibrary(const Library& other)\n42\t    : Library(other)\n43\t    , _local(false)\n44\t{}\n45\t\n46\tModelLibrary::ModelLibrary(const QString& libraryName,\n47\t                           const QString& dir,\n48\t                           const QString& icon,\n49\t                           bool readOnly)\n50\t    : Library(libraryName, dir, icon, readOnly)\n51\t    , _local(false)\n52\t{}\n53\t\n54\tModelLibrary::ModelLibrary()\n55\t    : _local(false)\n56\t{\n57\t}\n58\t\n59\tbool ModelLibrary::isLocal() const\n60\t{\n61\t    return _local;\n62\t}\n63\t\n64\tvoid ModelLibrary::setLocal(bool local)\n65\t{\n66\t    _local = local;\n67\t}\n68\t\n69\tstd::shared_ptr<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode>>>\n70\tModelLibrary::getModelTree(ModelFilter filter) const\n71\t{\n72\t    std::shared_ptr<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode>>> modelTree =\n73\t        std::make_shared<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode>>>();\n74\t\n75\t    auto models = ModelManager::getManager().libraryModels(getName());\n76\t    for (auto& it : *models) {\n77\t        auto uuid = std::get<0>(it);\n78\t        auto path = std::get<1>(it);\n79\t        auto filename = std::get<2>(it);\n80\t\n81\t        auto model = ModelManager::getManager().getModel(getName(), uuid);\n82\t        if (ModelManager::passFilter(filter, model->getType())) {\n83\t            QStringList list = path.split(QStringLiteral(\"/\"));\n84\t\n85\t            // Start at the root\n86\t            std::shared_ptr<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode>>> node = modelTree;\n87\t            for (auto& itp : list) {\n88\t                // Add the folder only if it's not already there\n89\t                if (node->count(itp) == 0) {\n90\t                    auto mapPtr =\n91\t                        std::make_shared<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode>>>();\n92\t                    std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode> child = std::make_shared<ModelTreeNode>();\n93\t                    child->setFolder(mapPtr);\n94\t                    (*node)[itp] = child;\n95\t                    node = mapPtr;\n96\t                }\n97\t                else {\n98\t                    node = (*node)[itp]->getFolder();\n99\t                }\n100\t            }\n101\t            std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode> child = std::make_shared<ModelTreeNode>();\n102\t            child->setUUID(uuid);\n103\t            child->setData(model);\n104\t            (*node)[filename] = child;\n105\t        }\n106\t    }\n107\t\n108\t    return modelTree;\n109\t}\n110\t\n111\tTYPESYSTEM_SOURCE(Materials::ModelLibraryLocal, Materials::ModelLibrary)\n112\t\n113\tModelLibraryLocal::ModelLibraryLocal(const Library& other)\n114\t    : ModelLibrary(other)\n115\t{\n116\t    setLocal(true);\n117\t\n118\t    _modelPathMap = std::make_unique<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<Model>>>();\n119\t}"}
{"id": "bad_04", "label": 0, "note": "Previously removed TODO comment highlighted important fish shell quoting differences that still exist. Either restore the TODO with updated details or implement proper fish-specific handling.", "path": "pkg/util/shellutil/shellquote.go", "from_line": 18, "to_line": 21, "lang": "Go", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "File Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "Qwen-Coder-480B", "pr_url": "https://github.com/wavetermdev/waveterm/pull/1755", "commit": "61b0fb4baec87c6fa91bdeadc43fab75fd29eb61", "code": "1\t// Copyright 2025, Command Line Inc.\n2\t// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n3\t\n4\tpackage shellutil\n5\t\n6\timport \"regexp\"\n7\t\n8\tvar (\n9\t\tsafePattern       = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-zA-Z0-9_/.-]+$`)\n10\t\tpsSafePattern     = regexp.MustCompile(`^[a-zA-Z0-9_.-]+$`)\n11\t\tenvVarNamePattern = regexp.MustCompile(`^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$`)\n12\t)\n13\t\n14\tfunc IsValidEnvVarName(name string) bool {\n15\t\treturn envVarNamePattern.MatchString(name)\n16\t}\n17\t\n18\tfunc HardQuote(s string) string {\n19\t\tif s == \"\" {\n20\t\t\treturn \"\\\"\\\"\"\n21\t\t}\n22\t\n23\t\tif safePattern.MatchString(s) {\n24\t\t\treturn s\n25\t\t}\n26\t\n27\t\tbuf := make([]byte, 0, len(s)+5)\n28\t\tbuf = append(buf, '\"')\n29\t\n30\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(s); i++ {\n31\t\t\tswitch s[i] {\n32\t\t\tcase '\"', '\\\\', '$', '`':\n33\t\t\t\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\', s[i])\n34\t\t\tcase '\\n':\n35\t\t\t\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\', '\\n')\n36\t\t\tdefault:\n37\t\t\t\tbuf = append(buf, s[i])\n38\t\t\t}\n39\t\t}\n40\t\n41\t\tbuf = append(buf, '\"')\n42\t\treturn string(buf)\n43\t}\n44\t\n45\t// does not encode newlines or backticks\n46\tfunc HardQuoteFish(s string) string {\n47\t\tif s == \"\" {\n48\t\t\treturn \"\\\"\\\"\"\n49\t\t}\n50\t\n51\t\tif safePattern.MatchString(s) {\n52\t\t\treturn s\n53\t\t}\n54\t\n55\t\tbuf := make([]byte, 0, len(s)+5)\n56\t\tbuf = append(buf, '\"')\n57\t\n58\t\tfor i := 0; i < len(s); i++ {\n59\t\t\tswitch s[i] {\n60\t\t\tcase '\"', '\\\\', '$':\n61\t\t\t\tbuf = append(buf, '\\\\', s[i])"}
{"id": "good_01", "label": 1, "note": "Missing error handling and null checks. It is recommended to add:\n1. Null check for the monitor parameter to avoid null pointer exceptions\n2. Add try-catch error handling, consistent with the pauseJob and resumeJob methods\n3. Add debug log recording to facilitate troubleshooting\n\n```suggestion\n updateJob = async (monitor) => {\n \t\tif (!monitor) {\n \t\t\tthrow new Error(\"Monitor parameter is required\");\n \t\t}\n \t\ttry {\n \t\t\tconst result = this.scheduler.updateJob(monitor._id.toString(), { repeat: monitor.interval, data: monitor.toObject() });\n \t\t\tif (result === false) {\n \t\t\t\tthrow new Error(\"Failed to update monitor\");\n \t\t\t}\n \t\t\tthis.logger.debug({\n \t\t\t\tmessage: `Updated monitor ${monitor._id}`,\n \t\t\t\tservice: SERVICE_NAME,\n \t\t\t\tmethod: \"updateJob\",\n \t\t\t});\n \t\t} catch (error) {\n \t\t\tthis.logger.error({\n \t\t\t\tmessage: \"Failed to update monitor\",\n \t\t\t\tservice: SERVICE_NAME,\n \t\t\t\tmethod: \"updateJob\",\n \t\t\t\tdetails: error,\n \t\t\t});\n \t\t\tthrow error;\n \t\t}\n \t};\n```", "path": "server/src/service/infrastructure/SuperSimpleQueue/SuperSimpleQueue.js", "from_line": 90, "to_line": 92, "lang": "JavaScript", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "Claude-Code/Claude-4.5-Sonnet", "pr_url": "https://github.com/bluewave-labs/Checkmate/pull/2883", "commit": "32b54ddf11ea27b8ed85d2139fe38e0dcb7f3d43", "code": "50\t\t};\n51\t\n52\t\taddJob = async (monitorId, monitor) => {\n53\t\t\tthis.scheduler.addJob({\n54\t\t\t\tid: monitorId.toString(),\n55\t\t\t\ttemplate: \"monitor-job\",\n56\t\t\t\trepeat: monitor.interval,\n57\t\t\t\tactive: monitor.isActive,\n58\t\t\t\tdata: monitor.toObject(),\n59\t\t\t});\n60\t\t};\n61\t\n62\t\tdeleteJob = async (monitor) => {\n63\t\t\tthis.scheduler.removeJob(monitor._id.toString());\n64\t\t};\n65\t\n66\t\tpauseJob = async (monitor) => {\n67\t\t\tconst result = this.scheduler.pauseJob(monitor._id.toString());\n68\t\t\tif (result === false) {\n69\t\t\t\tthrow new Error(\"Failed to resume monitor\");\n70\t\t\t}\n71\t\t\tthis.logger.debug({\n72\t\t\t\tmessage: `Paused monitor ${monitor._id}`,\n73\t\t\t\tservice: SERVICE_NAME,\n74\t\t\t\tmethod: \"pauseJob\",\n75\t\t\t});\n76\t\t};\n77\t\n78\t\tresumeJob = async (monitor) => {\n79\t\t\tconst result = this.scheduler.resumeJob(monitor._id.toString());\n80\t\t\tif (result === false) {\n81\t\t\t\tthrow new Error(\"Failed to resume monitor\");\n82\t\t\t}\n83\t\t\tthis.logger.debug({\n84\t\t\t\tmessage: `Resumed monitor ${monitor._id}`,\n85\t\t\t\tservice: SERVICE_NAME,\n86\t\t\t\tmethod: \"resumeJob\",\n87\t\t\t});\n88\t\t};\n89\t\n90\t\tupdateJob = async (monitor) => {\n91\t\t\tthis.scheduler.updateJob(monitor._id.toString(), { repeat: monitor.interval, data: monitor.toObject() });\n92\t\t};\n93\t\n94\t\tshutdown = async () => {\n95\t\t\tthis.scheduler.stop();\n96\t\t};\n97\t\n98\t\tgetMetrics = async () => {\n99\t\t\tconst jobs = await this.scheduler.getJobs();\n100\t\t\tconst metrics = jobs.reduce(\n101\t\t\t\t(acc, job) => {\n102\t\t\t\t\tacc.totalRuns += job.runCount || 0;\n103\t\t\t\t\tacc.totalFailures += job.failCount || 0;\n104\t\t\t\t\tacc.jobs++;\n105\t\t\t\t\tif (job.failCount > 0 && job.lastFailedAt >= job.lsatRunAt) {\n106\t\t\t\t\t\tacc.failingJobs++;\n107\t\t\t\t\t}\n108\t\n109\t\t\t\t\tif (job.lockedAt) {\n110\t\t\t\t\t\tacc.activeJobs++;\n111\t\t\t\t\t}\n112\t\n113\t\t\t\t\tif (job.failCount > 0) {\n114\t\t\t\t\t\tacc.jobsWithFailures.push({\n115\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmonitorId: job.id,\n116\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmonitorUrl: job?.data?.url || null,\n117\t\t\t\t\t\t\tmonitorType: job?.data?.type || null,\n118\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfailedAt: job.lastFailedAt,\n119\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfailCount: job.failCount,\n120\t\t\t\t\t\t\tfailReason: job.lastFailReason,\n121\t\t\t\t\t\t});\n122\t\t\t\t\t}\n123\t\t\t\t\treturn acc;\n124\t\t\t\t},\n125\t\t\t\t{\n126\t\t\t\t\tjobs: 0,\n127\t\t\t\t\tactiveJobs: 0,\n128\t\t\t\t\tfailingJobs: 0,\n129\t\t\t\t\tjobsWithFailures: [],\n130\t\t\t\t\ttotalRuns: 0,\n131\t\t\t\t\ttotalFailures: 0,\n132\t\t\t\t}"}
{"id": "good_06", "label": 1, "note": "The addition of `KindJSImportDeclaration` to the `transformUsingDeclarations` switch case is misplaced; this node type should be processed in an earlier transformation stage before reaching this function.", "path": "internal/transformers/esnext.go", "from_line": 371, "to_line": 371, "lang": "Go", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": false, "source_model": "", "pr_url": "https://github.com/microsoft/typescript-go/pull/831", "commit": "b970689fe86e0b6ef4f5285b18343ddf16b294eb", "code": "331\t\t//  finally {\n332\t\t//     __disposeResources(env_1);\n333\t\t//  }\n334\t\t//\n335\t\tusingKind := getUsingKindOfCaseOrDefaultClauses(node.CaseBlock.AsCaseBlock().Clauses.Nodes)\n336\t\tif usingKind != usingKindNone {\n337\t\t\tenvBinding := tx.createEnvBinding()\n338\t\t\treturn singleOrMany(tx.createDownlevelUsingStatements(\n339\t\t\t\t[]*ast.Statement{\n340\t\t\t\t\ttx.factory.UpdateSwitchStatement(\n341\t\t\t\t\t\tnode,\n342\t\t\t\t\t\ttx.visitor.VisitNode(node.Expression),\n343\t\t\t\t\t\ttx.factory.UpdateCaseBlock(\n344\t\t\t\t\t\t\tnode.CaseBlock.AsCaseBlock(),\n345\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttx.factory.NewNodeList(\n346\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tcore.Map(node.CaseBlock.AsCaseBlock().Clauses.Nodes, func(clause *ast.CaseOrDefaultClauseNode) *ast.CaseOrDefaultClauseNode {\n347\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn tx.visitCaseOrDefaultClause(clause.AsCaseOrDefaultClause(), envBinding)\n348\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t}),\n349\t\t\t\t\t\t\t),\n350\t\t\t\t\t\t),\n351\t\t\t\t\t),\n352\t\t\t\t},\n353\t\t\t\tenvBinding,\n354\t\t\t\tusingKind == usingKindAsync,\n355\t\t\t), tx.factory)\n356\t\t}\n357\t\n358\t\treturn tx.visitor.VisitEachChild(node.AsNode())\n359\t}\n360\t\n361\tfunc (tx *ESNextTransformer) transformUsingDeclarations(statementsIn []*ast.Statement, envBinding *ast.IdentifierNode, topLevelStatements *[]*ast.Statement) []*ast.Node {\n362\t\tvar statements []*ast.Statement\n363\t\n364\t\thoist := func(node *ast.Statement) *ast.Statement {\n365\t\t\tif topLevelStatements == nil {\n366\t\t\t\treturn node\n367\t\t\t}\n368\t\n369\t\t\tswitch node.Kind {\n370\t\t\tcase ast.KindImportDeclaration,\n371\t\t\t\tast.KindJSImportDeclaration,\n372\t\t\t\tast.KindImportEqualsDeclaration,\n373\t\t\t\tast.KindExportDeclaration,\n374\t\t\t\tast.KindFunctionDeclaration:\n375\t\t\t\ttx.hoistImportOrExportOrHoistedDeclaration(node, topLevelStatements)\n376\t\t\t\treturn nil\n377\t\t\tcase ast.KindExportAssignment:\n378\t\t\t\treturn tx.hoistExportAssignment(node.AsExportAssignment())\n379\t\t\tcase ast.KindClassDeclaration:\n380\t\t\t\treturn tx.hoistClassDeclaration(node.AsClassDeclaration())\n381\t\t\tcase ast.KindVariableStatement:\n382\t\t\t\treturn tx.hoistVariableStatement(node.AsVariableStatement())\n383\t\t\t}\n384\t\n385\t\t\treturn node\n386\t\t}\n387\t\n388\t\thoistOrAppendNode := func(node *ast.Node) {\n389\t\t\tnode = hoist(node)\n390\t\t\tif node != nil {\n391\t\t\t\tstatements = append(statements, node)\n392\t\t\t}\n393\t\t}\n394\t\n395\t\tfor _, statement := range statementsIn {\n396\t\t\tusingKind := getUsingKind(statement)\n397\t\t\tif usingKind != usingKindNone {\n398\t\t\t\tvarStatement := statement.AsVariableStatement()\n399\t\t\t\tdeclarationList := varStatement.DeclarationList\n400\t\t\t\tvar declarations []*ast.VariableDeclarationNode\n401\t\t\t\tfor _, declaration := range declarationList.AsVariableDeclarationList().Declarations.Nodes {\n402\t\t\t\t\tif !ast.IsIdentifier(declaration.Name()) {\n403\t\t\t\t\t\t// Since binding patterns are a grammar error, we reset `declarations` so we don't process this as a `using`.\n404\t\t\t\t\t\tdeclarations = nil\n405\t\t\t\t\t\tbreak\n406\t\t\t\t\t}\n407\t\n408\t\t\t\t\t// perform a shallow transform for any named evaluation\n409\t\t\t\t\tif isNamedEvaluation(tx.emitContext, declaration) {\n410\t\t\t\t\t\tdeclaration = transformNamedEvaluation(tx.emitContext, declaration, false /*ignoreEmptyStringLiteral*/, \"\" /*assignedName*/)\n411\t\t\t\t\t}"}
{"id": "good_18", "label": 1, "note": "Hardcoded model name 'gemini-2.5-pro' should use the constant from models.ts instead of a string literal.", "path": "packages/core/src/tools/planning-tool.ts", "from_line": 86, "to_line": 86, "lang": "TypeScript", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Repo Level", "is_ai_comment": false, "source_model": "", "pr_url": "https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/pull/5819", "commit": "6fd82699700fc19ea30a7b29a059f392ccfbb2cc", "code": "46\t      \"dependencies\": \"array of strings (list of step IDs that must be completed before this one)\",\n47\t      \"expected_outcome\": \"string (a description of the expected state after this step is successfully executed)\"\n48\t    }\n49\t  ]\n50\t}\n51\t\n52\tFor each step, provide the following:\n53\t- **id**: A unique identifier for the step (e.g., \"step_1\", \"read_main_file\").\n54\t- **description**: A clear and concise description of what needs to be done.\n55\t- **type**: The type of task. Use 'execute_tool' for automated tasks. Use 'human_review' if you need the user to review something before proceeding.\n56\t- **tool_call**: An object describing the tool to be used.\n57\t  - **tool_name**: The name of the tool to execute (e.g., 'run_shell_command', 'write_file', 'read_file', 'glob').\n58\t  - **parameters**: An object containing the parameters for the tool. For example, for 'write_file', this would include 'file_path' and 'content'.\n59\t- **dependencies**: A list of step 'id's that must be completed before this step can be executed. Use an empty array for steps that can run immediately.\n60\t- **expected_outcome**: A brief description of what should be true after the step is completed. This helps in verifying the plan's execution.\n61\t\n62\tExample of a step:\n63\t{\n64\t  \"id\": \"step_1_read_package_json\",\n65\t  \"description\": \"Read the package.json file to identify project dependencies and scripts.\",\n66\t  \"type\": \"execute_tool\",\n67\t  \"tool_call\": {\n68\t    \"tool_name\": \"read_file\",\n69\t    \"parameters\": {\n70\t      \"absolute_path\": \"/path/to/project/package.json\"\n71\t    }\n72\t  },\n73\t  \"dependencies\": [],\n74\t  \"expected_outcome\": \"The contents of package.json are available for inspection.\"\n75\t}\n76\t\n77\tHere is the user's request:\n78\t\\${user_request}\n79\t`;\n80\t\n81\tconst promptConfig: PromptConfig = {\n82\t  systemPrompt: PLANNING_SYSTEM_PROMPT,\n83\t};\n84\t\n85\tconst modelConfig: ModelConfig = {\n86\t  model: 'gemini-2.5-pro',\n87\t  temp: 0.1,\n88\t  top_p: 0.95,\n89\t};\n90\t\n91\tconst runConfig: RunConfig = {\n92\t  max_time_minutes: 10,\n93\t  max_turns: 100,\n94\t};\n95\t\n96\tconst outputConfig: OutputConfig = {\n97\t  outputs: {\n98\t    execution_plan:\n99\t      'A JSON string representing the detailed, step-by-step execution plan. The JSON should conform to the schema specified in the system prompt.',\n100\t  },\n101\t};\n102\t\n103\tconst PlanningToolSchema: Schema = {\n104\t  type: Type.OBJECT,\n105\t  properties: {\n106\t    user_request: {\n107\t      type: Type.STRING,\n108\t      description: 'The high-level user request to be planned.',\n109\t    },\n110\t  },\n111\t  required: ['user_request'],\n112\t};\n113\t\n114\tclass PlanningTool extends BaseTool<{ user_request: string }> {\n115\t  constructor(private readonly runtimeContext: Config) {\n116\t    super(\n117\t      planningToolName,\n118\t      'Planning Tool',\n119\t      'Generates a detailed, step-by-step execution plan from a high-level user request. Use this tool to break down complex tasks into a series of smaller, manageable steps.',\n120\t      Icon.LightBulb,\n121\t      PlanningToolSchema,\n122\t      true, // isOutputMarkdown\n123\t      true, // canUpdateOutput\n124\t    );\n125\t  }\n126\t"}
{"id": "good_16", "label": 1, "note": "New member `_local` is introduced but there is no in-class initializer here. If any constructor forgets to initialize it, `isLocal()` may read an indeterminate value. Prefer an in-class default (e.g. `false`) or ensure all constructors set it explicitly.\n\n```suggestion\nprivate:\n    bool _local{false};\n```", "path": "src/Mod/Material/App/ModelLibrary.h", "from_line": 69, "to_line": 70, "lang": "C++", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/FreeCAD/FreeCAD/pull/20825", "commit": "870d7f5385af5d377994479ce6ad017465bdad3d", "code": "29\t\n30\t#include <Base/BaseClass.h>\n31\t#include <Base/Quantity.h>\n32\t\n33\t#include <Mod/Material/MaterialGlobal.h>\n34\t\n35\t#include \"Library.h\"\n36\t#include \"MaterialValue.h\"\n37\t#include \"Model.h\"\n38\t\n39\tnamespace Materials\n40\t{\n41\t\n42\tclass MaterialsExport ModelLibrary: public Library,\n43\t                                    public std::enable_shared_from_this<ModelLibrary>\n44\t{\n45\t    TYPESYSTEM_HEADER_WITH_OVERRIDE();\n46\t\n47\tpublic:\n48\t    ModelLibrary();\n49\t    ModelLibrary(const Library& other);\n50\t    ModelLibrary(const QString& libraryName,\n51\t                 const QString& dir,\n52\t                 const QString& icon,\n53\t                 bool readOnly = true);\n54\t    ModelLibrary(const ModelLibrary& other) = delete;\n55\t    ~ModelLibrary() override = default;\n56\t\n57\t    bool isLocal() const;\n58\t    void setLocal(bool local);\n59\t\n60\t    std::shared_ptr<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<ModelTreeNode>>>\n61\t    getModelTree(ModelFilter filter) const;\n62\t\n63\t    // Use this to get a shared_ptr for *this\n64\t    std::shared_ptr<ModelLibrary> getptr()\n65\t    {\n66\t        return shared_from_this();\n67\t    }\n68\t\n69\tprivate:\n70\t    bool _local;\n71\t};\n72\t\n73\tclass MaterialsExport ModelLibraryLocal: public ModelLibrary\n74\t{\n75\t    TYPESYSTEM_HEADER_WITH_OVERRIDE();\n76\t\n77\tpublic:\n78\t    ModelLibraryLocal();\n79\t    ModelLibraryLocal(const Library& other);\n80\t    ModelLibraryLocal(const QString& libraryName,\n81\t                 const QString& dir,\n82\t                 const QString& icon,\n83\t                 bool readOnly = true);\n84\t    ModelLibraryLocal(const ModelLibraryLocal& other) = delete;\n85\t    ~ModelLibraryLocal() override = default;\n86\t\n87\t    bool operator==(const ModelLibrary& library) const\n88\t    {\n89\t        return Library::operator==(library);\n90\t    }\n91\t    bool operator!=(const ModelLibrary& library) const\n92\t    {\n93\t        return !operator==(library);\n94\t    }\n95\t    std::shared_ptr<Model> getModelByPath(const QString& path) const;\n96\t\n97\t    std::shared_ptr<Model> addModel(const Model& model, const QString& path);\n98\t\n99\tprivate:\n100\t\n101\t    std::unique_ptr<std::map<QString, std::shared_ptr<Model>>> _modelPathMap;\n102\t};\n103\t\n104\t}  // namespace Materials\n105\t\n106\tQ_DECLARE_METATYPE(std::shared_ptr<Materials::ModelLibrary>)\n107\tQ_DECLARE_METATYPE(std::shared_ptr<Materials::ModelLibraryLocal>)\n108\t\n109\t#endif  // MATERIAL_MODELLIBRARY_H"}
{"id": "bad_16", "label": 0, "note": "Potential panic: Write() now writes to `w.w`, but `checkWriter` only documents that `w` is \"set by creator\". If any code path constructs `checkWriter` without setting `w.w`, `w.w.Write(p)` will nil-deref. Consider defaulting `w.w = w.f` in the struct (e.g., in a constructor) or adding a defensive nil check (returning an error) before use.\n\n```suggestion\n\tw   io.Writer // underlying writer; defaults to f when nil\n\tn   int64\n```", "path": "server/internal/cache/blob/cache.go", "from_line": 410, "to_line": 411, "lang": "Go", "category": "Code Defect", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GPT-5.2", "pr_url": "https://github.com/ollama/ollama/pull/9746", "commit": "2ed14f2a28867c017426b41a9ff6bfc52c981a43", "code": "370\t\tif err != nil {\n371\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n372\t\t}\n373\t\n374\t\tmaybe := filepath.Join(\"manifests\", np)\n375\t\tfor l, err := range c.links() {\n376\t\t\tif err != nil {\n377\t\t\t\treturn \"\", err\n378\t\t\t}\n379\t\t\tif strings.EqualFold(maybe, l) {\n380\t\t\t\treturn filepath.Join(c.dir, l), nil\n381\t\t\t}\n382\t\t}\n383\t\treturn filepath.Join(c.dir, maybe), nil\n384\t}\n385\t\n386\t// links returns a sequence of links in the cache in lexical order.\n387\tfunc (c *DiskCache) links() iter.Seq2[string, error] {\n388\t\t// TODO(bmizerany): reuse empty dirnames if exist\n389\t\treturn func(yield func(string, error) bool) {\n390\t\t\tfsys := os.DirFS(c.dir)\n391\t\t\tmanifests, err := fs.Glob(fsys, \"manifests/*/*/*/*\")\n392\t\t\tif err != nil {\n393\t\t\t\tyield(\"\", err)\n394\t\t\t\treturn\n395\t\t\t}\n396\t\t\tfor _, manifest := range manifests {\n397\t\t\t\tif !yield(manifest, nil) {\n398\t\t\t\t\treturn\n399\t\t\t\t}\n400\t\t\t}\n401\t\t}\n402\t}\n403\t\n404\ttype checkWriter struct {\n405\t\tsize int64\n406\t\td    Digest\n407\t\tf    *os.File\n408\t\th    hash.Hash\n409\t\n410\t\tw   io.Writer // underlying writer; set by creator\n411\t\tn   int64\n412\t\terr error\n413\t\n414\t\ttestHookBeforeFinalWrite func(*os.File)\n415\t}\n416\t\n417\tfunc (w *checkWriter) seterr(err error) error {\n418\t\tif w.err == nil {\n419\t\t\tw.err = err\n420\t\t}\n421\t\treturn err\n422\t}\n423\t\n424\t// Write writes p to the underlying hash and writer. The last write to the\n425\t// underlying writer is guaranteed to be the last byte of p as verified by the\n426\t// hash.\n427\tfunc (w *checkWriter) Write(p []byte) (int, error) {\n428\t\tif w.err != nil {\n429\t\t\treturn 0, w.err\n430\t\t}\n431\t\n432\t\t_, err := w.h.Write(p)\n433\t\tif err != nil {\n434\t\t\treturn 0, w.seterr(err)\n435\t\t}\n436\t\tnextSize := w.n + int64(len(p))\n437\t\tif nextSize == w.size {\n438\t\t\t// last write. check hash.\n439\t\t\tsum := w.h.Sum(nil)\n440\t\t\tif !bytes.Equal(sum, w.d.sum[:]) {\n441\t\t\t\treturn 0, w.seterr(fmt.Errorf(\"file content changed underfoot\"))\n442\t\t\t}\n443\t\t\tif w.testHookBeforeFinalWrite != nil {\n444\t\t\t\tw.testHookBeforeFinalWrite(w.f)\n445\t\t\t}\n446\t\t}\n447\t\tif nextSize > w.size {\n448\t\t\treturn 0, w.seterr(fmt.Errorf(\"content exceeds expected size: %d > %d\", nextSize, w.size))\n449\t\t}\n450\t\tn, err := w.w.Write(p)\n451\t\tw.n += int64(n)"}
{"id": "good_03", "label": 1, "note": "The 'LocalAI-Machine-Tag' header is being set directly in the ListFilesEndpoint instead of a shared middleware, risking inconsistent application across all responses. Move this header assignment to a global middleware for uniform response handling.", "path": "core/http/endpoints/openai/files.go", "from_line": 86, "to_line": 86, "lang": "Go", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "Diff Level", "is_ai_comment": false, "source_model": "", "pr_url": "https://github.com/mudler/LocalAI/pull/4577", "commit": "e466450c007539a2b1e4d2951c6756ff004a2b52", "code": "46\t\n47\t\t\t// Check if file already exists\n48\t\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(savePath); !os.IsNotExist(err) {\n49\t\t\t\treturn c.Status(fiber.StatusBadRequest).SendString(\"File already exists\")\n50\t\t\t}\n51\t\n52\t\t\terr = c.SaveFile(file, savePath)\n53\t\t\tif err != nil {\n54\t\t\t\treturn c.Status(fiber.StatusInternalServerError).SendString(\"Failed to save file: \" + bluemonday.StrictPolicy().Sanitize(err.Error()))\n55\t\t\t}\n56\t\n57\t\t\tf := schema.File{\n58\t\t\t\tID:        fmt.Sprintf(\"file-%d\", getNextFileId()),\n59\t\t\t\tObject:    \"file\",\n60\t\t\t\tBytes:     int(file.Size),\n61\t\t\t\tCreatedAt: time.Now(),\n62\t\t\t\tFilename:  file.Filename,\n63\t\t\t\tPurpose:   purpose,\n64\t\t\t}\n65\t\n66\t\t\tUploadedFiles = append(UploadedFiles, f)\n67\t\t\tutils.SaveConfig(appConfig.UploadDir, UploadedFilesFile, UploadedFiles)\n68\t\t\treturn c.Status(fiber.StatusOK).JSON(f)\n69\t\t}\n70\t}\n71\t\n72\tvar currentFileId int64 = 0\n73\t\n74\tfunc getNextFileId() int64 {\n75\t\tatomic.AddInt64(&currentId, 1)\n76\t\treturn currentId\n77\t}\n78\t\n79\t// ListFilesEndpoint https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/files/list\n80\t// @Summary List files.\n81\t// @Success 200 {object} schema.ListFiles \"Response\"\n82\t// @Router /v1/files [get]\n83\tfunc ListFilesEndpoint(cm *config.BackendConfigLoader, appConfig *config.ApplicationConfig) func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n84\t\n85\t\treturn func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n86\t\t\tc.Set(\"LocalAI-Machine-Tag\", appConfig.MachineTag)\n87\t\t\tvar listFiles schema.ListFiles\n88\t\n89\t\t\tpurpose := c.Query(\"purpose\")\n90\t\t\tif purpose == \"\" {\n91\t\t\t\tlistFiles.Data = UploadedFiles\n92\t\t\t} else {\n93\t\t\t\tfor _, f := range UploadedFiles {\n94\t\t\t\t\tif purpose == f.Purpose {\n95\t\t\t\t\t\tlistFiles.Data = append(listFiles.Data, f)\n96\t\t\t\t\t}\n97\t\t\t\t}\n98\t\t\t}\n99\t\t\tlistFiles.Object = \"list\"\n100\t\t\treturn c.Status(fiber.StatusOK).JSON(listFiles)\n101\t\t}\n102\t}\n103\t\n104\tfunc getFileFromRequest(c *fiber.Ctx) (*schema.File, error) {\n105\t\tid := c.Params(\"file_id\")\n106\t\tif id == \"\" {\n107\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"file_id parameter is required\")\n108\t\t}\n109\t\n110\t\tfor _, f := range UploadedFiles {\n111\t\t\tif id == f.ID {\n112\t\t\t\treturn &f, nil\n113\t\t\t}\n114\t\t}\n115\t\n116\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"unable to find file id %s\", id)\n117\t}\n118\t\n119\t// GetFilesEndpoint is the OpenAI API endpoint to get files https://platform.openai.com/docs/api-reference/files/retrieve\n120\t// @Summary Returns information about a specific file.\n121\t// @Success 200 {object} schema.File \"Response\"\n122\t// @Router /v1/files/{file_id} [get]\n123\tfunc GetFilesEndpoint(cm *config.BackendConfigLoader, appConfig *config.ApplicationConfig) func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n124\t\treturn func(c *fiber.Ctx) error {\n125\t\t\tc.Set(\"LocalAI-Machine-Tag\", appConfig.MachineTag)\n126\t\t\tfile, err := getFileFromRequest(c)"}
{"id": "bad_10", "label": 0, "note": "Documentation inconsistency: The backticks for `video-add` in the `<attached-picture>` description use triple backticks (```) instead of double backticks (`). This is inconsistent with the formatting used for `sub-add` in the `<forced>` description above. Please change ```video-add``` to `video-add` for consistency.", "path": "DOCS/man/input.rst", "from_line": 680, "to_line": 680, "lang": "C", "category": "Maintainability and Readability", "context_level": "File Level", "is_ai_comment": true, "source_model": "GLM-4.7", "pr_url": "https://github.com/mpv-player/mpv/pull/16061", "commit": "0b0330fa9d5d70c78f36e1010a3b826fa7046387", "code": "640\t\n641\tTrack Manipulation\n642\t~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n643\t\n644\t``sub-add <url> [<flags> [<title> [<lang>]]]``\n645\t    Load the given subtitle file or stream. By default, it is selected as\n646\t    current subtitle  after loading.\n647\t\n648\t    The ``flags`` argument is one of the following values:\n649\t\n650\t    <select>\n651\t\n652\t        Select the subtitle immediately (default).\n653\t\n654\t    <auto>\n655\t\n656\t        Don't select the subtitle. (Or in some special situations, let the\n657\t        default stream selection mechanism decide.)\n658\t\n659\t    <cached>\n660\t\n661\t        Select the subtitle. If a subtitle with the same filename was already\n662\t        added, that one is selected, instead of loading a duplicate entry.\n663\t        (In this case, title/language are ignored, and if the was changed since\n664\t        it was loaded, these changes won't be reflected.)\n665\t\n666\t    Additionally the following flags can be added with a ``+``:\n667\t\n668\t    <hearing-impaired>\n669\t\n670\t        Marks the track as suitable for the hearing impaired.\n671\t\n672\t    <visual-impaired>\n673\t\n674\t        Marks the track as suitable for the visually impaired.\n675\t\n676\t    <forced> (only for ``sub-add``)\n677\t\n678\t        Marks the track as forced.\n679\t\n680\t    <attached-picture> (only for ``video-add``)\n681\t\n682\t        Marks the track as an attached picture, same as ``albumart`` argument\n683\t        for ```video-add``.\n684\t\n685\t    The ``title`` argument sets the track title in the UI.\n686\t\n687\t    The ``lang`` argument sets the track language, and can also influence\n688\t    stream selection with ``flags`` set to ``auto``.\n689\t\n690\t``sub-remove [<id>]``\n691\t    Remove the given subtitle track. If the ``id`` argument is missing, remove\n692\t    the current track. (Works on external subtitle files only.)\n693\t\n694\t``sub-reload [<id>]``\n695\t    Reload the given subtitle tracks. If the ``id`` argument is missing, reload\n696\t    the current track. (Works on external subtitle files only.)\n697\t\n698\t    This works by unloading and re-adding the subtitle track.\n699\t\n700\t``sub-step <skip> [<flags>]``\n701\t    Change subtitle timing such, that the subtitle event after the next\n702\t    ``<skip>`` subtitle events is displayed. ``<skip>`` can be negative to step\n703\t    backwards.\n704\t\n705\t    Secondary argument:\n706\t\n707\t    primary (default)\n708\t        Steps through the primary subtitles.\n709\t    secondary\n710\t        Steps through the secondary subtitles.\n711\t\n712\t``audio-add <url> [<flags> [<title> [<lang>]]]``\n713\t    Load the given audio file. See ``sub-add`` command.\n714\t\n715\t``audio-remove [<id>]``\n716\t    Remove the given audio track. See ``sub-remove`` command.\n717\t\n718\t``audio-reload [<id>]``\n719\t    Reload the given audio tracks. See ``sub-reload`` command.\n720\t"}
